Portable Plex Prep Scripts

Startup menu flow
- Running `video-convert.ps1` with no mode now shows:
  1) Hardware Test
  2) Encode TV Show
  3) Encode Movies
- Choosing 2 or 3 prompts for the media root path before encoding starts.

Main scripts
- `video-convert.ps1` (interactive menu + compatibility entrypoint)
- `scripts/Start-TV.ps1` (mode 1 / 720p TV profile)
- `scripts/Start-Movies.ps1` (mode 2 / 1080p Movies profile)
- `scripts/Ensure-Dependencies.ps1` (downloads/refreshes toolchain)

Portable dependency management
- `-EnsureDependencies` verifies/downloads missing tools into `tools\` (only the needed components for the selected flow).
- Dependency downloads now show human-readable progress (percent, transferred size, speed, ETA).
- `-RefreshDependencies` forces a re-download/update even when tools already exist.

Backup behavior
- `Originals` folders are created only when `-BackupOriginal` is enabled.
- Without `-BackupOriginal`, originals are removed after successful replacement and no empty backup folders are left behind.

Hardware test + cache
- Selecting Hardware Test from the menu automatically enables dependency bootstrap (HandBrake only).
- `-ProbeHardwareOnly` runs GPU/encoder capability probe and exits.
- `-RefreshHardwareCache` forces refresh of probe data.
- Cache file: `Config\hardware-profile-<COMPUTERNAME>.json`.
- Auto mode (`-EncoderMode Auto`) reuses cached profile when valid.

Completed CSV behavior
- Completed records are stored with full input/output paths.
- At end of each run, the completed CSV is rewritten as a clean snapshot (one latest row per input path) to keep resume data tidy and avoid wasted re-processing.

Typical usage
1) Menu-driven:
`powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\video-convert.ps1`

2) TV pass:
`powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\Start-TV.ps1 -RootPath "Y:\TV Shows" -EnsureDependencies -EnableFileBotRename`

3) Movies pass:
`powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\Start-Movies.ps1 -RootPath "Y:\Movies" -EnsureDependencies -EnableFileBotRename`

4) Hardware test only:
`powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\video-convert.ps1 -ProbeHardwareOnly -RefreshHardwareCache`


PowerShell ISE / console run notes
- Do **not** wrap the command in backticks. Backticks in PowerShell are escape characters, not quote wrappers.
- From an open PowerShell prompt in the repo folder, use either:
  - `& ".\video-convert.ps1"`
  - `powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ".\video-convert.ps1"`
- Or use the Windows helper launcher (avoids command formatting mistakes):
  - `run-video-convert.cmd`
- To pass args through the cmd launcher:
  - `run-video-convert.cmd -ProbeHardwareOnly -RefreshHardwareCache`


Diagnostics
- Each launcher run writes a session transcript log under `Logs\Session-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.log` for troubleshooting.
- Run `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\Test-PowerShellSyntax.ps1` to pre-check for parser errors / unexpected tokens before running jobs.
